":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Restart DSH. The `academic_writing` tool is registered host-wide."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Tool"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| action | purpose |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| `outline` | Paper outline skeleton (research / review / proposal / essay), optional section cap |\n"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"| `title` | Title variants from style templates (descriptive, question, declarative, colon) |\n| `abs"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"tract` | Structured abstract skeleton — background / methods / results / conclusion |\n| `citation` |"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" Reference entry formatted as **GB/T 7714**, **APA 7**, or **MLA 9** |\n| `check` | Phrasing QA on a "},{"id":"p11s5","text":"passage (passive voice, first person, hedging, sentence length) |\n| `checklist` | Pre-submission che"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"cklist (ethics, conflict of interest, data, funding, formatting) |\n| `references` | Reference list f"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"rom citation entries — deduplicated and sorted (GB/T 7714 / APA / MLA) |\n| `latex` | LaTeX snippets:"},{"id":"p11s8","text":" booktabs table, equation (inline/display/align), code listing, thebibliography |\n| `structure` | Ma"},{"id":"p11s9","text":"nuscript structure check — heading levels, paragraph budget, outline coverage |\n| `glossary` | Term/"},{"id":"p11s10","text":"abbreviation glossary with first-occurrence definitions |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Config"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"All optional, on the composition row's `config`:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| key | default | meaning |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| `personaSection` | `true` | register the academic prompt-guidance section |\n| `sectionOrder` | `6`"},{"id":"p15s2","text":" | prompt section order (persona is 0, ascending) |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Design"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Pure logic (`lib/academic.js`) has zero DSH/Cordis imports and is unit-tested in isolation; `lib/ind"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"ex.js` is the thin Cordis plugin wiring the tool and the prompt section. No filesystem access — ever"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"ything is deterministic and side-effect free."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"MIT"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Roadmap"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"See ROADMAP.md — next five versions (v0.2.0 – v0.6.0): reference management, structure QA, expressio"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"n risk, journal adaptation, review workflow."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
